{"files":[{"content":"#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    long int start;\n    long int count;\n    long int next;\n} bucket;\n\nstatic void sort_bucket(char *strings, long int *indices, long int *scratch,\n                        long int start, long int count, int length) {\n    long int *src = indices;\n    long int *dst = scratch;\n    long int width;\n\n    for (width = 1; width < count; ) {\n        long int end = start + count;\n        long int left = start;\n\n        while (left < end) {\n            long int remaining = end - left;\n            long int mid = left + (width < remaining ? width : remaining);\n            long int right_remaining = end - mid;\n            long int right = mid + (width < right_remaining ? width : right_remaining);\n            long int i = left;\n            long int j = mid;\n            long int out = left;\n\n            while (i < mid && j < right) {\n                if (strcmp(strings + src[i] * length,\n                           strings + src[j] * length) <= 0) {\n                    dst[out++] = src[i++];\n                } else {\n                    dst[out++] = src[j++];\n                }\n            }\n            while (i < mid)\n                dst[out++] = src[i++];\n            while (j < right)\n                dst[out++] = src[j++];\n\n            left = right;\n        }\n\n        {\n            long int *tmp = src;\n            src = dst;\n            dst = tmp;\n        }\n\n        if (width > count / 2)\n            width = count;\n        else\n            width *= 2;\n    }\n\n    if (src != indices)\n        memcpy(indices + start, src + start, (size_t)count * sizeof(*indices));\n}\n\nstatic long int *bucket_sort(char *strings, int length, long int size,\n                             int offset, int nbuckets) {\n    long int *indices;\n    long int *scratch;\n    bucket *buckets;\n    long int i;\n    long int total = 0;\n\n    if (size == 0)\n        return NULL;\n\n    indices = (long int *)malloc((size_t)size * sizeof(*indices));\n    scratch = (long int *)malloc((size_t)size * sizeof(*scratch));\n    buckets = (bucket *)calloc((size_t)nbuckets, sizeof(*buckets));\n    if (indices == NULL || scratch == NULL || buckets == NULL) {\n        free(indices);\n        free(scratch);\n        free(buckets);\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Unable to allocate bucket-sort storage\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        int bucket_index = (int)(unsigned char)strings[i * length] - offset;\n        buckets[bucket_index].count++;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++) {\n        buckets[i].start = total;\n        buckets[i].next = total;\n        total += buckets[i].count;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        int bucket_index = (int)(unsigned char)strings[i * length] - offset;\n        buckets[bucket_index].next++;\n        indices[buckets[bucket_index].next - 1] = i;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < nbuckets; i++)\n        sort_bucket(strings, indices, scratch, buckets[i].start,\n                    buckets[i].count, length);\n\n    free(scratch);\n    free(buckets);\n    return indices;\n}\n\nstatic void load(char **strings_out, long int *size_out, int *length_out,\n                 int *offset_out, int *nbuckets_out) {\n    char *strings;\n    int length;\n    int offset;\n    int nbuckets;\n    long int size;\n    long int i;\n\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &length) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"ERROR len\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &size) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"ERROR n\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"ERROR offset\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    if (fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbuckets) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    nbuckets++;\n    length++;\n    strings = (char *)malloc((size_t)size * (size_t)length);\n    if (strings == NULL && size != 0) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"Unable to allocate input storage\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n        if (fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + i * length) != 1) {\n            fprintf(stderr, \"ERROR %ld\\n\", i);\n            free(strings);\n            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n        }\n    }\n\n    *strings_out = strings;\n    *size_out = size;\n    *length_out = length;\n    *offset_out = offset;\n    *nbuckets_out = nbuckets;\n}\n\nstatic void save(char *strings, long int *indices, long int size, int length) {\n    long int i;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < size; i++)\n        printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + indices[i] * length);\n}\n\nint main(void) {\n    char *strings = NULL;\n    long int size = 0;\n    long int *indices = NULL;\n    int length = 0;\n    int offset;\n    int nbuckets;\n\n    load(&strings, &size, &length, &offset, &nbuckets);\n    indices = bucket_sort(strings, length, size, offset, nbuckets);\n    save(strings, indices, size, length);\n\n    free(strings);\n    free(indices);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n","path":"src/bucketsort.c"}],"hypothesis":"Replacing per-bucket insertion sort with stable bottom-up mergesort removes quadratic behavior for large buckets. Counting and prefix-packing bucket indices into contiguous ranges, then merging through a reusable scratch array, should also improve sequential memory access while preserving strcmp ordering.","notes":"Unmeasured candidate; the controller should evaluate correctness and speed. Bucket ranges are sized from observed counts, so uneven bucket populations do not rely on fixed per-bucket capacity.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Count records per bucket and prefix-sum counts to create exact contiguous bucket ranges.","Scatter indices into those ranges in input order.","Sort each range with stable iterative mergesort using one reusable scratch array and strcmp comparisons."]}